@@ -0,0 +1,85 @@
+# Bootfile Studio operating service
+
+This service prepares Bootfile Marketing Setup drafts and can provide a five-minute heartbeat to the application's bounded paid-order runner. A third capability triggers the application’s independent owned-blog review and limited publisher. All three capabilities are **off by default**. Social publication, repository writes, ad spending, and outbound prospecting are outside this service.
+
+The application is the durable source of draft and paid-order state. Generation stops when its draft ledger cannot be checked. A completed draft is pending review, never implicitly approved or published.
+
+## Product contract
+
+The offer is **$49 once** for a solo service-business owner: one promotion becomes a customer email and three coordinated social posts, accompanied by a saved business brief, a reusable task setup, and a quality checklist. `/studio` is the entry point. `src/product.ts` contains the shared brief used by every generation task. Legacy profile copy, quiz links, invented outcomes, and guaranteed revenue are outside that brief.
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Variable | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `GROWTH_DRAFTS_ENABLED=true` | Explicitly enable draft schedules after the application ingress is verified |
+| `BOOTFILE_APP_URL` | Exact reviewed HTTPS application origin, without a path/query/fragment |
+| `GROWTH_AGENT_SECRET` | Newly configured dedicated draft-ingress credential, matching the application |
+| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | Existing approved generation account |
+| `PERPLEXITY_API_KEY` | Existing approved research account |
+| `GROWTH_MODEL` | Optional generation model, existing default `claude-sonnet-4-6` |
+| `BLOG_CRON` | UTC blog draft cadence; default Monday/Thursday 09:00 |
+| `INSTAGRAM_CRON` | UTC caption draft cadence; default Tuesday/Friday 12:00 |
+| `RESEARCH_CRON` | UTC research-note cadence; default Monday 06:00 |
+| `OPERATIONS_SCHEDULER_ENABLED=true` | Explicitly enable the separate paid-operations heartbeat |
+| `BOOTFILE_OPERATIONS_URL` | Exact reviewed HTTPS `/api/operations/run` endpoint |
+| `BOOTFILE_CRON_SECRET` | Newly configured dedicated credential matching the app's `CRON_SECRET` |
+| `GROWTH_PUBLISHER_ENABLED=true` | Enable the separate owned-blog operating trigger after release validation |
+| `BOOTFILE_PUBLISHER_URL` | Exact reviewed HTTPS `/api/operations/publish` endpoint |
+| `GROWTH_PUBLISHER_SECRET` | Dedicated publisher credential, separate from draft/admin/cron credentials |
+| `PUBLISHER_CRON` | UTC check cadence, default `15 */6 * * *`; database review/publication caps apply |
+
+No GitHub token or Meta credential is required by this implementation. Remove unused write credentials only through the normal credential-management process after this version is verified. Do not retrieve old credentials from another platform to work around missing hosting access.
+
+`BOOTFILE_OPERATIONS_URL` is trusted deployment configuration, never generated content. Redirects are refused so credentials cannot be forwarded to a different endpoint. A hostname change is a reviewed deployment change.
+
+## What runs
+
+Content tasks share one execution lane, so this single service instance does not run multiple content jobs at once. Each blog/caption is limited to one persisted draft per UTC day; research is limited to one persisted note per UTC week. The application checks the deterministic key before the service calls a model, then persists the result with a unique key. Restarting the service does not trigger a content burst.
+
+The default cadence creates up to two blog drafts, two caption drafts, and one research note per week. Existing Railway schedule variables override defaults; set them deliberately during activation. A provider call has a timeout and token ceiling. A failed response or invalid structured output stops the task. There is no recursive research fallback and no fail-open editorial decision.
+
+The optional operations heartbeat runs every five minutes in its own guarded lane. It calls the app's existing authenticated routine endpoint and records the returned status. The app enforces batch limits, durable leases, refunds, and run deduplication. The service never receives customer intake or payment credentials through this response.
+
+Application-level idempotency prevents duplicate drafts and duplicate paid work. Keep this service at one replica unless a distributed scheduling/claim mechanism is introduced; a read-before-generate draft check is not a distributed model-spend lock.
+
+## Implemented owned-blog policy and owner involvement
+
+During release validation, keep application publication disabled. The application can independently review drafts with `GROWTH_REVIEW_ENABLED=true` while `GROWTH_PUBLICATION_ENABLED=false`; approved articles remain private. Once the concrete release checks pass, routine publication follows the operating charter without a daily owner queue. Material policy, product, security, or spending changes remain owner decisions.
+
+The application implements these boundaries:
+
+- Its `/api/operations/publish` route accepts only a trigger authenticated with the dedicated publisher secret. The service cannot submit an approval, arbitrary public body, or target URL. The author’s draft credential cannot authorize this route.
+- A private database claim reserves an exact draft hash and a four-minute lease before a paid review. There are at most **two review claims per rolling seven days**, including failed or unknown attempts. No recursive repair or model retry loop exists.
+- Deterministic checks allow only current-product article drafts with a fixed source link, bounded content, clearly fictional examples, and the current $49 price. Raw HTML, images, unapproved links, old quiz/pricing language, and unsupported guarantees are rejected before public rendering.
+- The application checks the current `https://bootfile.ai/studio` page, without credentials or redirects. A fresh reviewer call receives server-owned product facts, the source excerpt, the proposed public fields, and recent articles. It has no author conversation history or action tools. Every mandatory check must pass, including useful new substance, supported facts, safe guidance, and no unconsented marketing.
+- Review approval binds the exact source hash and stores the exact normalized article with its own database hash. Changed source content, a changed approved article, an expired approval, or an existing public slug prevents publication.
+- A separate transaction can publish only the stored approved article to the owned `blog_posts` table. It never overwrites an existing slug. A durable cap allows at most **two publication events per rolling seven days**, including subsequently withdrawn articles.
+- Completed approvals can resume publication without another model call. Ordinary editorial rejections remain unpublished. Provider failures, unknown reviews, and other operating exceptions enter the private ledger for agent investigation; they are not instructions for Nick to review every draft.
+- An authenticated operator may withdraw only the exact article published by this pipeline, preserving its private audit and original body. Withdrawal refuses an article subsequently changed by another editor. The growth credential cannot perform withdrawals.
+
+The app’s required publication configuration is `GROWTH_PUBLISHER_SECRET`, `GROWTH_REVIEW_ENABLED=false`, `GROWTH_PUBLICATION_ENABLED=false`, the existing `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, and optional `GROWTH_REVIEW_MODEL` (default `claude-sonnet-4-6`). The separate publisher migration and its rollback-only smoke live in the application repository. No enabling flag or committed code is evidence of a live deployed publisher.
+
+## Activation and proof
+
+1. Deploy the application branch, apply its reviewed migrations, and verify `/api/operations/drafts` and `/api/operations/run` with the intended production configuration.
+2. Configure new scoped credentials on both sides using the authorized provider surfaces. Keep all enable flags false while checking configuration.
+3. Run `npm ci`, `npm run build`, and `npm test`. Verify no credentialless call or startup can dispatch work.
+4. Configure the selected schedules and enable the required capability. Do not enable both native Vercel five-minute cron and Railway heartbeat without understanding that the shared run key will skip duplicates.
+5. Observe two unattended paid-operation invocations in `operations_runs`. Test draft persistence and ensure it appears pending in `/admin` without a repository push or public article.
+6. Validate the publication failure gates and separate credentials. Observe an independent review with public writes disabled, then verify one controlled publication and exact withdrawal through the application’s reviewed release process. Enable routine owned-blog publication only after these checks pass.
+7. Record the Railway deployment ID/source SHA, enabled capabilities, schedule evidence, and the app deployment SHA. Only then describe the service as active.
+
+If the host's plan supports only daily native cron, this optional Railway heartbeat provides the required five-minute trigger after explicit endpoint/credential configuration. Check the actual hosting plan and provider docs; do not assume that a schedule file proves a supported or running cadence.
+
+## Build and rollback
+
+The release dependency review found no high/critical production advisory; a moderate `node-cron` 3 / `uuid` dependency issue remains. Cron expressions are trusted deployment configuration. A breaking scheduler upgrade needs its own focused validation; no forced audit rewrite is part of this change.
+
+`npm run build` compiles TypeScript. `npm test` runs deterministic URL, cadence-key, and credential-forwarding boundary checks without calling any external provider.
+
+Pause the affected capability with its enable flag. Set the app’s `GROWTH_PUBLICATION_ENABLED=false` to stop public writes independently of the Railway trigger. If paid operations need to stop, also consider the app's `BOOTFILE_OPERATIONS_PAUSED` and checkout controls. Do not roll back to the old auto-publishing service while leaving its write credentials active; that version had a direct-to-master publication path.
+
+## Baseline inspected
+
+This rebuild was prepared from the connected repository's `master` ref `f92b48de0da38522ff80bc7728e90f92454ad7d7`, inspected 2026-10-20. CLI clone lacked repository credentials, so the local source was hydrated through the authorized GitHub connection. No live Railway configuration or publication was changed while preparing it.
